I've been trying to get 3.1 to make on my PC and have had some 
problems.  I followed all of the instructions, and everything 
actually compiles (MSC 7.0), but when it goes to link it all
together, ZILLIONS of error messages (well, maybe not zillions)
are generated until it finally ends with:

LINK : fatal error L2041: stack plus data exceed 64K

The error messages that fly by are mostly symbols defined more
than once (error L2025).  It seems that when each file is
compiled with the /DOVL1, /DOVL2, etc. compiler line
parameters, the data which should only be compiled on certain
passes is actually being compiled every time.  An example is:

.\o\attrib.1(attrib.c) : error L2025: _attrmax : symbol defined more than once
.\o\attrib.1(attrib.c) : error L2025: _attrmin : symbol defined more than once
.\o\attrib.1(attrib.c) : error L2025: _adjattrib : symbol defined more than once

	and on and on...

Any suggestions?

